; A floating-point number is no truth value either: `x as bool` went through
; the signed conversion to one bit, so `2.0 as bool` was false at rc 0
; (2026-11-10). Planner.report_bool_cast#.
; xfail: cast of a f64 to bool

function truth(x: f64) returns bool
    x as bool

if truth(2.0) = false
    print "PASS"
